@startuml RestroVibes - Rating System
!theme plain
title RestroVibes - Bidirectional Rating System

actor Client
actor Restaurateur
participant "Express API" as API
participant "PostgreSQL" as DB

== CLIENT RATES RESTAURATEUR ==

Client -> API : POST /api/ratings/\n{ appointmentId: 42,\ntargetType: "restaurateur",\nscore: 5,\ncomment: "Great food and service!" }
API -> DB : Verify appointment exists\nand status = "completed"
API -> DB : Check unique constraint:\n(clientId, appointmentId, targetType)\nNo duplicate allowed
API -> DB : INSERT INTO ratings\n(appointmentId, clientId,\ntargetId, targetType,\nscore, comment)
DB --> API : Rating created
API -> DB : SELECT AVG(score)\nFROM ratings\nWHERE targetType = "restaurateur"\nAND targetId = restaurateurId
DB --> API : avg = 4.5, count = 12
API --> Client : 201 { rating, average: 4.5 }

== RESTAURATEUR RATES CLIENT ==

Restaurateur -> API : POST /api/ratings/\n{ appointmentId: 42,\ntargetType: "client",\nscore: 4,\ncomment: "Good customer" }
API -> DB : Verify appointment exists\nand status = "completed"
API -> DB : Check unique constraint:\n(restaurateurId, appointmentId, "client")
API -> DB : INSERT INTO ratings\n(appointmentId, restaurateurId,\ntargetId, targetType,\nscore, comment)
DB --> API : Rating created
API -> DB : SELECT AVG(score)\nFROM ratings\nWHERE targetType = "client"\nAND targetId = clientId
DB --> API : avg = 4.2, count = 8
API --> Restaurateur : 201 { rating, average: 4.2 }

== VIEW RATINGS FOR APPOINTMENT ==

Client -> API : GET /api/ratings/appointment/:appointmentId
API -> DB : SELECT * FROM ratings\nWHERE appointmentId = :id
DB --> API : [{ targetType: "restaurateur",\nscore: 5 },\n{ targetType: "client",\nscore: 4 }]
API --> Client : { ratings: [...] }

== GET AVERAGE RATING ==

Client -> API : GET /api/ratings/average/restaurateur/:id
API -> DB : SELECT AVG(score), COUNT(*)\nFROM ratings\nWHERE targetType = 'restaurateur'\nAND targetId = :id
DB --> API : { avg: 4.5, count: 12 }
API --> Client : { average: 4.5, count: 12 }

Restaurateur -> API : GET /api/ratings/average/client/:id
API -> DB : SELECT AVG(score), COUNT(*)\nFROM ratings\nWHERE targetType = 'client'\nAND targetId = :id
DB --> API : { avg: 4.2, count: 8 }
API --> Restaurateur : { average: 4.2, count: 8 }

== CONSTRAINTS ==

note over API,DB
  - One rating per appointment per direction
  - Score range: 1-5 stars
  - Ratings only after appointment completed
  - Enforced by unique DB constraint on
    (appointmentId, clientId/targetId, targetType)
end note

@enduml
